= Large language model — Technical =

== Sequence model ==
For token sequence x_1,...,x_n, an autoregressive LM factorizes:

<pre>
P(x_1:n) = Π_t P(x_t | x_<t)
</pre>

Training commonly minimizes token-level negative log-likelihood over large corpora.

Masked/bidirectional language models optimize related conditional reconstruction objectives.

== Scale ==
“Large” can refer jointly to:

<pre>
parameter count
training-token count
compute
model width/depth
context length
capability regime
</pre>

and has no invariant numerical threshold.

== Adaptation ==
A pretrained LLM can be adapted through:

* supervised fine-tuning;
* instruction tuning;
* preference optimization;
* reinforcement learning;
* retrieval augmentation;
* tool interfaces;
* parameter-efficient tuning;
* prompting/in-context conditioning.

These are system/training procedures, not part of the minimal definition of an LLM.

== Agent boundary ==
An agent architecture adds state/action semantics around a model:

<pre>
LLM
+ controller
+ tools/actions
+ memory/state
+ environment feedback
≠ LLM alone
</pre>

